WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.271
Detection engineering is the discipline of creating and maintaining visibility into suspicious, risky, or policy-relevant activity.

2
00:00:08.271 --> 00:00:20.125
Detection engineers design capabilities that help organizations identify threats, investigate alerts, and improve defensive awareness before small signals become larger problems.

3
00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:26.700
Although people often associate detection engineering with writing SIEM queries, the discipline is much broader.

4
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:36.887
It includes telemetry planning, threat-informed design, testing, documentation, tuning, lifecycle management, measurement, and continuous improvement.

5
00:00:36.887 --> 00:00:39.432
A detection is not just a line of logic.

6
00:00:39.432 --> 00:00:48.821
It is a maintained defensive asset that depends on data quality, context, alert presentation, investigation guidance, ownership, and a plan for review.

7
00:00:48.821 --> 00:00:54.009
If any of those pieces are missing, analysts may receive noise instead of useful signal.

8
00:00:54.009 --> 00:00:59.587
Detection engineering gives security teams a repeatable way to ask important defensive questions.

9
00:00:59.587 --> 00:01:00.934
What activity matters?

10
00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:02.281
What data can show it?

11
00:01:02.281 --> 00:01:03.878
How will the alert be tested?

12
00:01:03.878 --> 00:01:06.023
What should analysts do when it fires?

13
00:01:06.023 --> 00:01:08.967
How will the team know whether the detection is still useful?

14
00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:10.474
The purpose is practical.

15
00:01:10.474 --> 00:01:22.457
Detection engineering helps defenders turn messy operational data into meaningful visibility, so teams can investigate faster, prioritize better, and learn from what they observe in their environment.

16
00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:26.757
A mature detection engineering program also creates shared language.

17
00:01:26.757 --> 00:01:37.234
Instead of debating alerts one at a time, teams can discuss coverage, fidelity, ownership, dependencies, review dates, response guidance, and measurable outcomes.

18
00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:41.634
That shift matters because security operations is under constant pressure.

19
00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:51.193
Detection engineering gives teams a structured way to improve visibility while respecting the limits of analyst time, platform performance, and business context.
